00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.060
is holding all of her pens and pencils.
用来装她所有钢笔和铅笔的。

454
00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.980
And then she has her pink mug that she's drinking out of.
然后她还有一个正在喝水的粉色马克杯。

455
00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:17.320
But I spotted that Pratt mug.
但我发现了那个普拉特学院的马克杯。

456
00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:17.780
Aw.
噢。

457
00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:20.580
That's a great detail from our set decoration crew.
那是我们布景装饰组的一个很棒的细节。

458
00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.820
Well, I love that.
嗯，我很喜欢这个。

459
00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:27.760
I was way in the corner, back by Stanley's file cabinet, and that was just trying to get
我当时在角落里，就在斯坦利的档案柜旁边，那是为了让我

460
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:28.540
me in the shot.
出现在镜头里。

461
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.440
Ken Quapis had me come out from accounting.
肯·夸皮斯让我从会计部走出来。

462
00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.660
Once again, I'm standing.
再一次，我站着。

463
00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:32.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

464
00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:34.400
And that's how we could all be there.
这就是我们所有人都能出现在那里的原因。

465
00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:38.280
Well, now we have our super short opening credits.
好了，现在我们有了超短的片头字幕。

466
00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:40.300
They are like 10 seconds.
大概只有10秒钟。

467
00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:45.280
Jen Salata did an interview with Office Tally, and she said they cut the credits down to get
简·萨拉塔接受了《办公室记分牌》的采访，她说他们缩减了片头字幕以争取

468
00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.560
more time for the episode.
更多的时间给剧集本身。

469
00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:52.280
She mentioned that they had gone back and forth about maybe making this episode an hour, but
她提到他们曾反复讨论过是否要把这一集做成一小时的特别篇，但

470
00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:53.900
she said they didn't feel like they needed it.
她说他们觉得没必要。

471
00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:58.520
There were other season finales, like The Job or Goodbye, Toby, where they had, like, tons
在其他季终集里，比如《工作》或《再见，托比》，他们有大量的

472
00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:02.040
of plot points to wrap up and huge moves they were going to make.
情节要收尾，还有重大的变动要发生。

473
00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:06.560
But in this episode, she said they didn't have that much.
但这一集，她说他们没有那么多内容。

474
00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:12.340
They just had kind of the one big move with Jim and Pam and a little bit of a move for Michael
他们只有吉姆和帕姆的一个大动作，以及迈克尔

475
00:22:12.340 --> 00:22:12.840
and Holly.
和霍莉的一点点进展。

476
00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.820
And then the rest of us, just little nods to our storylines.
至于我们其他人，只是对我们的故事线做了一些小小的呼应。

477
00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:20.320
Yeah, but she said they did need to steal that little bit of time from the credits.
是的，但她说他们确实需要从片头字幕里偷出那一点点时间。

478
00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:21.900
The day has arrived.
这一天终于到了。

479
00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.540
It is the Dunder Mifflin Company Picnic.
这是邓德·米夫林公司的野餐日。

480
00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.780
Here's a breakdown of all the different branches and their t-shirts.
这是所有不同分部及其T恤颜色的明细。

481
00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:29.520
Oh!
噢！

482
00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:31.040
Thank you, Dunderpedia.
谢谢你，邓德百科。

483
00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:33.600
I started making notes, and then I saw you had it.
我刚开始做笔记，就看到你已经整理好了。

484
00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:36.480
So I'm going to read what you have.
所以我打算读一下你整理的内容。

485
00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:43.920
Corporate, black t-shirts, Akron yellow, Albany light blue, Buffalo orange, Nashua green,
总公司是黑色T恤，阿克伦是黄色，奥尔巴尼是浅蓝色，布法罗是橙色，纳舒厄是绿色，

486
00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:48.760
Rochester dark purple, Scranton red, and Utica dark blue.
罗切斯特是深紫色，斯克兰顿是红色，尤蒂卡是深蓝色。

487
00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:52.720
Lady, I'm calling this episode The Plain Hats Club.
女士，我把这一集称为“素色帽子俱乐部”。

488
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:59.180
Oh, I can't wait to hear this, because I have some lingo I made up for this episode as well.
噢，我迫不及待想听听这个了，因为我也为这一集编了一些术语。

489
00:22:59.320 --> 00:23:02.000
Everyone in this episode is wearing a plain hat.
这一集里的每个人都戴着素色的帽子。

490
00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:06.300
And that is because if you wear a logo anywhere on your shirt or your hat,
这是因为如果你在衬衫或帽子上戴了任何标志，

491
00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:09.340
the production has to get it cleared with that company firSt.
制作组必须先获得该公司的许可。

492
00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:13.280
So I have a breakdown of everyone's plain hat.
所以我有一个关于每个人戴的素色帽子的明细。

493
00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:15.320
Like the plain baseball hats?
是指那种素色的棒球帽吗？

494
00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:15.780
Yes!
是的！

495
00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:19.440
Jim is wearing a plain black baseball hat.
吉姆戴着一顶素色的黑色棒球帽。

496
00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:21.140
Pam has a white visor.
帕姆戴着一个白色的遮阳帽。

497
00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:26.980
Dwight has a tan fishing hat, which I googled and I learned is called a bucket hat.
德怀特戴着一顶棕褐色的渔夫帽，我查了谷歌，才知道它叫桶帽。

498
00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:27.620
Hmm.
嗯。

499
00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:30.820
Kevin is also wearing a tan bucket hat.
凯文也戴着一顶棕褐色的桶帽。

500
00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:33.460
Angela has a floppy sun hat.
安吉拉戴着一顶软檐遮阳帽。

501
00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.220
Andy has a tan Panama hat.
安迪戴着一顶棕褐色的巴拿马草帽。

502
00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:39.880
Aaron has a sort of light purple baseball hat.
亚伦戴着一顶浅紫色的棒球帽。

503
00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:42.460
Creed has a light tan baseball hat.
克里德戴着一顶浅棕色的棒球帽。

504
00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:44.640
Ryan has a white visor.
瑞安戴着一个白色的遮阳帽檐。

505
00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.320
Stanley has a straw sun hat.
斯坦利戴着一顶草编遮阳帽。

506
00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:53.440
Phyllis has no hat while she's playing volleyball, but she has a straw sun hat on the sidelines.
菲利斯打排球时没戴帽子，但在场边时戴着一顶草编遮阳帽。

507
00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:55.240
Meredith has no hat.
梅雷迪思没戴帽子。

508
00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.280
Oscar has no hat.
奥斯卡没戴帽子。

509
00:23:58.020 --> 00:24:02.660
Charles Minor has a black Nike visor.
查尔斯·迈纳戴着一个黑色的耐克遮阳帽檐。

510
00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:04.120
How did we get away with that?
我们是怎么蒙混过关的？

511
00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:05.200
I don't know!
我不知道！

512
00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:06.100
Because it's Idris.
因为那是伊德里斯。

513
00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:08.800
And we're just like, let Idris do what he wants to do.
我们当时就想，让伊德里斯做他想做的事吧。

514
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:10.580
We're just glad to have you back.
我们很高兴你能回来。

515
00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:11.640
I don't know.
我不知道。

516
00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:15.780
Toby also has a yellow baseball hat with a logo.
托比也戴着一顶带标志的黄色棒球帽。

517
00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:18.520
It has little trees, but I couldn't read what it was.
上面有小树的图案，但我看不清写的是什么。

518
00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:22.860
Well, you know, part of the hat strategy was because it got so hot during the day.
嗯，你知道，戴帽子的策略部分是因为白天太热了。

519
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.080
We needed it.
我们需要它。

520
00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:32.620
We needed it when we were playing volleyball as well to kind of create a shade on our faces so that you could see our expressions.
我们在打排球时也需要它，为了给脸部遮阳，这样你们才能看清我们的表情。

521
00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:36.800
So we weren't completely blown out by the sun, also for sun protection.
这样我们就不会被阳光完全晃得睁不开眼，也是为了防晒。

522
00:24:37.240 --> 00:24:40.520
But you might notice that Michael and Holly do not wear hats.
但你们可能注意到迈克尔和霍莉没戴帽子。

523
00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:45.260
They are mostly in their cutesy little, like, love neSt.
他们大多待在他们那可爱的小爱巢里。

524
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.180
Shady tree area.
树荫区。

525
00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:47.280
Yeah, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

526
00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:49.580
Well, Jenna, I also did a little bit of tracking.
好吧，珍娜，我也做了一点追踪调查。

527
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:55.380
I want you to know that I feel like this episode really brings out some of our characters' other traits.
我想让你知道，我觉得这一集真的展现了我们角色身上的一些其他特质。

528
00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:57.300
Oh, I made a liSt.
哦，我列了个清单。

529
00:24:57.560 --> 00:25:10.880
We have Sporty Pam, Saucy Jim, Petty Charles, Trash Talking Andy, Snarky Michael, and my most favorite, Vacation Stanley.
我们有运动型帕姆、风流吉姆、小气的查尔斯、爱说垃圾话的安迪、尖酸刻薄的迈克尔，还有我最喜欢的度假模式斯坦利。

530
00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:13.560
I love Vacation Stanley.
我爱度假模式的斯坦利。

531
00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.920
So the picnic starts with Pam and Jim.
野餐从帕姆和吉姆开始。

532
00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:22.940
They're walking up, and they share a little bit about what last year's softball company picnic was like.
他们走过来，分享了一些关于去年公司垒球野餐的情况。

533
00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:27.100
Jim had that spider in his mitt, but that's not what Pam is talking about.
吉姆的手套里有那只蜘蛛，但帕姆说的不是这个。

534
00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:31.180
She's talking about the guy who grabbed her boobs to keep his balance.
她说的是那个为了保持平衡而抓她胸部的家伙。

535
00:25:31.740 --> 00:25:32.420
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

536
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:37.500
And then Pam points at her chest and says, yeah, you don't grab these for balance.
然后帕姆指着自己的胸部说，没错，你可不能为了保持平衡抓这些地方。

537
00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:39.540
And Jim goes, well.
吉姆回了句，好吧。

538
00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:41.860
And this is Saucy Jim.
这就是风流吉姆。

539
00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:48.540
Well, next up, Dwight arrives with his friend, Rolf.
接下来，德怀特带着他的朋友罗尔夫到了。

540
00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:50.200
His best friend.
他最好的朋友。

541
00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:58.460
And who they met at a shoe store when Dwight overheard Rolf asking for a shoe that would increase his speed but not leave any tracks.
他们是在一家鞋店认识的，当时德怀特无意中听到罗尔夫在问有没有能增加速度但不会留下脚印的鞋子。

542
00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:00.220
These two are made for each other.
这两人真是天造地设的一对。

543
00:26:00.580 --> 00:26:02.700
We had a fan question from David H.
我们收到一个来自宾夕法尼亚州大卫·H的粉丝提问。

544
00:26:02.820 --> 00:26:03.440
in Pennsylvania.
在宾夕法尼亚州。

545
00:26:03.700 --> 00:26:05.160
Who played Dwight's friend?
是谁扮演了德怀特的朋友？

546
00:26:05.460 --> 00:26:07.760
Was he somehow related to the show already?
他之前就和这部剧有什么关联吗？

547
00:26:08.220 --> 00:26:12.280
Guys, Rolf was played by the amazing James Urbaniac.
伙计们，罗尔夫是由了不起的詹姆斯·乌尔巴尼亚克扮演的。

548
00:26:12.580 --> 00:26:13.600
And get this, Ange.
而且你听着，安吉。

549
00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:13.920
What?
什么？

550
00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:17.600
He auditioned and was called back for the role of Dwight.
他参加了试镜，并被召回参加了德怀特这个角色的复试。

551
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:20.200
Well, that makes perfect sense to me.
嗯，这对我来说完全说得通。

552
00:26:20.440 --> 00:26:20.780
Doesn't it?
不是吗？

553
00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:24.040
He and Rain knew each other from their New York theater days.
他和雷恩在纽约演艺圈时期就认识了。

554
00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:29.360
And after Rain read this script, he called James and gave him a heads up.
雷恩读完剧本后，给詹姆斯打了电话，提前知会了他一声。

555
00:26:30.040 --> 00:26:33.420
And he told Greg, you need to bring in James Urbaniac for this.
他还告诉格雷格，你得找詹姆斯·乌尔巴尼亚克来演这个角色。

556
00:26:33.520 --> 00:26:35.540
Well, they knew him because they had auditioned him.
嗯，他们认识他，因为他们之前面试过他。

557
00:26:35.740 --> 00:26:37.660
So he went in to see Allison Jones.
于是他去见了艾莉森·琼斯。

558
00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:39.120
He read for the role.
他试读了这个角色。

559
00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:49.260
Ken talked a little bit in the DVD commentary about just how perfectly cast James was and that for a guest star to come in on such a big episode,
肯在DVD评论音轨里稍微提到了詹姆斯的选角有多么完美，对于一个客串演员来说，能在一集这么重要的剧集里登场，

560
00:26:49.880 --> 00:26:54.020
James just fit in so seamlessly you would have never known he had never been on the show before.
詹姆斯融入得如此天衣无缝，你根本看不出他之前从未上过这个节目。

561
00:26:54.220 --> 00:26:59.020
That is just how organic his performance was and that he just crushed it.
他的表演就是这么自然，而且他演得太棒了。

562
00:26:59.020 --> 00:27:04.040
Well, he's one of those guys who's been a working actor for a very, very long time.
嗯，他是那种做了很久很久职业演员的人。

563
00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:10.000
And I feel like he's one of those people where you recognize him immediately from his body of work.
我觉得他属于那种你一看他的作品集就能立刻认出来的人。

564
00:27:10.080 --> 00:27:10.620
He's a pro.
他是个专业人士。

565
00:27:10.980 --> 00:27:13.540
We got this interesting letter from Jana M.
我们收到了一封来自Jana M.的有趣来信，

566
00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:16.060
in Westport County, Mayo, Ireland.
她住在爱尔兰梅奥郡的韦斯特波特。

567
00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:17.260
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

568
00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:18.820
We have letters from everywhere.
我们收到了来自世界各地的信件。

569
00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:20.160
This is so exciting to me.
这让我太兴奋了。

570
00:27:20.340 --> 00:27:23.780
You know, we added a feature on the website where you can say where you're writing from.
你知道，我们在网站上增加了一个功能，你可以标注你写信的地点。

571
00:27:23.940 --> 00:27:24.940
I love that.
我喜欢这个功能。

572
00:27:24.940 --> 00:27:29.260
I know, me too, because it's really fun to see how international the show is.
我也是，因为看到这个节目有多么国际化真的很有趣。

573
00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:29.520
I know.
我知道。

574
00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:33.580
Well, when we get mail here to Earwolf that I open, I can always see where people are from.
嗯，当我们在Earwolf收到邮件并拆开时，我总能看到人们来自哪里。

575
00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:35.840
But before in emails, we weren't always sure.
但以前在电子邮件里，我们并不总是确定。

576
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:37.720
Here is what Jana said.
这是Jana说的内容。

577
00:27:38.040 --> 00:27:49.280
Fun fact, James Urbaniak, the actor who played Dwight's best friend Rolf, whom he met in a shoe store, also played a shoe store employee with a foot fetish on Sex and the City.
有趣的事实：饰演德怀特最好的朋友罗尔夫的演员詹姆斯·乌尔巴尼亚克，也就是德怀特在鞋店认识的那个人，也曾在《欲望都市》里饰演过一个有恋足癖的鞋店员工。

578
00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:53.000
What is it about James Urbaniak in shoe stores?
詹姆斯·乌尔巴尼亚克和鞋店到底有什么缘分？

579
00:27:53.580 --> 00:27:54.600
That's really funny.
那真的很有趣。

580
00:27:54.600 --> 00:27:55.600
I think that's fun.
我觉得这很有意思。

581
00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:57.460
And now Christine B.
现在是克里斯汀·B.

582
00:27:57.740 --> 00:27:59.880
from Mississippi asked this.
来自密西西比州的她问了这个问题。

583
00:28:00.120 --> 00:28:05.580
I've heard that Rolf was introduced because Moe's was busy on Parks and Rec.
我听说罗尔夫这个角色的引入是因为莫斯当时在忙《公园与游憩》的拍摄。

584
00:28:05.780 --> 00:28:06.900
Is that true?
这是真的吗？

585
00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.040
Oh, savvy question.
哦，真是个精明的问题。

586
00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:10.480
It is true.
这是真的。

587
00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:15.880
You guys, originally, Moe's was supposed to come to the picnic with Dwight.
伙计们，最初莫斯本应该和德怀特一起去野餐的。

588
00:28:15.880 --> 00:28:21.540
And they called up Mike Schur, who was now running Parks and Rec.
他们给当时正在负责《公园与游憩》的迈克·舒尔打了电话。

589
00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:28.380
And the week we shot Company Picnic, he was directing an episode of Parks and Rec as well as running the show.
在我们拍摄《公司野餐》那一周，他不仅在负责那部剧，还在导演《公园与游憩》的一集。

